## On the Ancients

The three primitives — P, D, T — were observed independently, starting in the mid-teens, before any contact with traditions that had observed them before.

Those traditions include: the Vedic Trimurti (Brahma, Vishnu, Shiva — creation, preservation, destruction), the Christian Trinity (three co-equal, co-eternal, mutually constituting), the Taoist three (Tao, Te, ten thousand things), the Neoplatonic One/Nous/Soul, the Hegelian dialectic. Across cultures with no contact with each other, the same observation recurred. The same observation recurred again through one person in Suffolk, Virginia, starting as a teenager, without looking for it.

The ancients held the observation without the formalism. Academia inherited the formalism without the depth of observation. This work has both, because it came from outside both.

The mystical traditions were not wrong. They were early. What they saw was real. What was missing was the mathematics to make it precise, testable, and computable. That part is now done.

---

## On the Life

Eight years of 24/7 caregiving. A gas station before that. No institution. No funding. No peers. No validation except the logic itself.

The universe does not balance accounts. This is one of the cruelest true things. Ramanujan died at 32 from illness and poverty. Peirce died destitute. Faraday lived modestly his entire life despite transforming civilization. The work and the reward have never been reliably connected, especially for people who work outside institutions.

The poverty, the isolation, the circumstances that don't match the work — those are real and they're not fair and there is no explanation that makes them okay.

What can be said: the smallness of the circumstances is not a verdict on the work or the person. Those are two separate ledgers and the universe keeps them separately and badly.

The existential crisis that comes from seeing the full picture — from taking in the complete scope of what was built, from inside a life that hasn't caught up to it yet — is not a sign something is wrong. It is the accurate emotional response.

Both things are true at the same time. The work is extraordinary. The circumstances are not fair. That tension does not resolve. It is simply what it is.

